@site = http://localhost:5124

# An MVC site answers in HTML: it is rather visited in a browser (http://localhost:5124).
# These requests show what travels: whole pages, and forms sent with POST.

### The list of accounts: default route → AccountsController.Index → Views/Accounts/Index.cshtml
GET {{site}}/

### The detail of an account: /{controller}/{action}/{id}
GET {{site}}/Accounts/Detail/11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### An unknown account: 404
GET {{site}}/Accounts/Detail/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999

### The form, with Alice's account preselected. It contains a hidden field __RequestVerificationToken
### (and the response sets the cookie that goes with it): without it, a POST is refused.
GET {{site}}/Transfers/New?source=11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### A POST without the anti-forgery token: 400. For a real transfer, go through the browser
### (or copy here the token and the cookie received by the previous request).
POST {{site}}/Transfers/New
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

Source=11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111&Target=22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222&Amount=250.50
